WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.977
TinyWifiDongle turns

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.571
an ESP32-S3 or

00:00:04.383 --> 00:00:05.880
Raspberry Pi Pico

00:00:05.704 --> 00:00:06.670
W board

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:09.316
Phil Schatzmann's MIT-licensed

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.838
Arduino library bridges

00:00:10.649 --> 00:00:11.934
a microcontroller's

00:00:11.746 --> 00:00:13.055
Wi-Fi to USB

00:00:12.866 --> 00:00:14.081
CDC-NCM

00:00:14.211 --> 00:00:15.059
so Linux

00:00:15.095 --> 00:00:16.545
macOS and Windows

00:00:16.357 --> 00:00:17.206
11 see a

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.491
network adapter without

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.446
extra drivers

00:00:19.966 --> 00:00:21.027
The board forwards

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:21.899
Ethernet frames at

00:00:21.711 --> 00:00:22.808
Layer 2 between

00:00:22.619 --> 00:00:24.116
USB and Wi-Fi

00:00:24.341 --> 00:00:25.237
so the computer

00:00:25.049 --> 00:00:25.874
gets its own

00:00:25.685 --> 00:00:26.546
IP from the

00:00:26.358 --> 00:00:27.925
router via DHCP

00:00:27.737 --> 00:00:29.057
with no NAT

00:00:29.582 --> 00:00:30.513
The author notes

00:00:30.325 --> 00:00:31.893
occasional USB stalls

00:00:31.705 --> 00:00:34.204
on the ESP32-S3

00:00:34.016 --> 00:00:36.280
after 100 to 200 MB

00:00:36.139 --> 00:00:37.435
and one unexplained

00:00:37.247 --> 00:00:38.178
Pico reboot

00:00:38.273 --> 00:00:39.369
and Windows 10

00:00:39.193 --> 00:00:40.183
needs an extra

00:00:39.995 --> 00:00:40.678
driver

00:00:41.214 --> 00:00:42.228
Full story on

00:00:42.039 --> 00:00:42.935
the dashboard
